WEBVTT

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.830
The story until now.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.510
"The culprit is among us,”

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.380
said Madame Mantis.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.800
Nozomu, hearing this, awakens in the lobby of an old Western mansion.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.590
In his right hand is a paper knife stained red with blood.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:29.270
In his left a ticket to Senior Freeter Night.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:36.120
Thinking that, with an abundance of evidence, he can catch the true culprit,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:42.390
he heads to the place written on the ticket, Shinjuku Loft Plus One.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.610
Raised on an unexpected dance platform,

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:50.500
even though he is questioned in an
interview setting about metrosexualism,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:59.060
the large-eared crowd in the VIP box chant for him to leave.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:35.000
When watching anime, wear proper clothes and sit properly.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.010
Go Go Fight Pro Baseball Relay!

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:47.180
And they enter the 6th with the score still nothing.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.050
I think he lives another life.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.790
Here comes the pitch!

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.550
What do you mean?

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.400
Oh, wow. Even though he's a top-notch pitcher, he looks like a model.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.700
That's why I think so.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.320
What if just because of his talent for baseball,

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.270
his potential for a fabulous life as a model has gone to waste?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.480
Isn't pro baseball successful enough?

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.390
We don't know if he would have been even more of a success as a model!

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.520
If he hadn't have played baseball,

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.380
we may have seen Darvish shine even brighter!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.970
Ganaha from the J-League, too;

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.900
were he only not so talented at soccer!

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.620
I'm sure he would be a great success as a member of Da Pump!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.510
Even Shokotan, were she not so cute!

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:41.770
Nowadays, unmistakably, as a cover author for Magazine J, she'd sell over 50,000,000 books total!

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:48.060
Even though their lives may be fabulous, they had other lives too.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.480
Thinking of it is somehow heartrending.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.030
If Manabe's breasts were bigger,

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.450
maybe she could've made it as a TV announcer.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.450
No boobs!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.710
You've grown up, Majiru.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:01.950
Really?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.740
Melancholy of Majiru!

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:07.110
Majiru, when you grow up, what do you want to be?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.170
Kids say the darnedest things.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.200
No, really!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.950
This is a bit sudden, but I have some Western-style sweets.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:18.720
Would you like some?

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.520
Hey, these are really tasty!

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.180
Aren't they?

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.680
The boss of that place made them.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:35.890
The guy from the sushi restaurant?

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.990
His sushi's incredibly tasty.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.730
But what if he wasn't any good at making sushi? See?

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.030
They say that heaven grants you only one gift.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.170
But in reality, some people get two or three.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:51.450
That messes up the proverb!

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.980
All of you with two or three gifts!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.110
Go back to properly having one, like heaven granted you!

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.810
Shall I make your body unable to play baseball!?

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.710
Hold it!

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.260
Or would you like to have the kind of face they can only draw in the comics!?

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.230
Don't!

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.020
Chiri, you're too quick to violence.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.940
It's only cut 38!

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.960
Even if you don't do that, Kitsu, Japan will be fine.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.640
It's not that heaven won't give you two gifts,

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.580
but that society will refuse to recognize two gifts!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.420
Japanese love that kind of compartmentalization!

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.900
They won't recognize a second gift that also pops up!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.550
You'd think he could be a #4 pitcher even in the pros.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.910
But society surely won't accept it!

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:37.790
When Ichiro wanted to pitch at the All-Star game, he was criticized for being rude!

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:40.130
Even though his fastball is nearly 150km/h!

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.790
And the boss of that place, were he to put these Western sweets out officially,

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:48.030
even if it didn't change, he'd be criticized for letting the quality of his sushi drop, wouldn't he.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.990
I kind of get it.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:55.600
But there's plenty of multi-talents on TV. Aren't they recognized?

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:57.100
Well,

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.000
None of their talents are recognized!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.010
I thought I was going to say it!

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.410
Because they do plenty, but it feels like it can all be summed up.

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.700
Hey, hey.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.910
Yes, a second talent that springs up truly won't be recognized.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.180
This is the tragedy of those who have too much!

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:19.160
I wanted to see their other lives, too!

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.390
They sound interesting.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.590
You were there?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.760
Always.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.270
I don't know if you can see it on days like today.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.770
Ah, there it is.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.600
The Twin Towers of Talent.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.460
One tower is for talents accepted by society.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.380
The other tower is for talents left unshown.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.510
If we go there,

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:46.220
we'll be able to see the other talent of those gifted twice!

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.620
Let's go!

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:52.090
You're just as strange as Tamori.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.090
Sure am.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:58.230
Everyone, behold!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.230
That's!

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.400
Ichiro the pitcher!

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:05.070
I almost gave up!

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.160
And Suzuki the announcer, popular among kids as a pro gamer!

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:17.150
Yes, this is a place where second talents that weren't let out into the light of society can blossom.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:18.920
Welcome!

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.750
Isn't it great, boss?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.960
Here I can use all the cream I want, like I love to do!

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.260
That's!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.440
If he didn't become a politican, just like that,

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.920
we'd have been able to see Putin take gold!

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.460
And if Kazushige hadn't played baseball,

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.720
wouldn't he have made a wonderful fighter?

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:42.170
With those muscles he'd have been quite pressed.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.260
What muscles?

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.360
You can see other second talents, too!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.870
If he didn't become Japan's PM,

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.100
he'd have blossomed as a Chinese politician!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.610
Without her extraordinary kiss power,

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.570
she'd have blossomed as a newscaster!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.430
If he didn't do track and field,

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.740
he'd have an investment office in the Hills!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.730
If he didn't tame animals,

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:07.050
he'd have made a name for himself as a pro mahjong player!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.420
If it had used DVDs!

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.790
If it had been based on the game!

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.650
If it had been produced by Kyoto!

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.510
If it had been serialized by Company S!

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:17.880
If he hadn't become assistant to the wrong man!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.830
So, shall we go to the next floor?

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:25.730
Here, those who have the dilemma of opposite talents

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.590
can allow their unshown talent to blossom!

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.540
She's a top-class SM queen, but!

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.590
She also has potential to be a top-class masochist!

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:39.620
But her clients don't recognize it!

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.100
Well, I guess.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:43.240
By becomeing a top-class masochist?

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.470
doesn't that make you not a top-class sadist?

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.110
That's why her talents cause a dilemma!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.080
There are more capabilities that cause dilemmas here!

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.360
A clever airheaded celeb!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.360
Ummmmmmmm...

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.150
An economy sedan that goes fast if you floor it!

00:08:56.150 --> 00:09:01.490
Certainly, for any of them, the appeal of one side damages the image of the other.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:05.140
It's like how hamburgers targeted at health fanatics didn't sell.

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:09.490
It truly can be thought of as having too many gifts.

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:14.630
You're lucky to have been spared from having any.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.050
Hey, that's rude!

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.140
Okay, next is the top floor!

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.280
The final boss!?

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:28.690
Harumi!

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:33.320
Didn't you take today off from school because of the deadline for your doujin?

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.390
Doujin? What's that?

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:37.060
It's this! Have you forgotten!?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.330
The Fujiyoshi that's here isn't the comics-nerd Fujiyoshi in glasses we're used to.

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:44.970
This is the Fujiyoshi that allowed her second and third talents to blossom!

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.300
Amazing!

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:50.470
I'd like a match with the famous sports elite Fujiyoshi!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.630
She took her glasses off!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:56.470
Those weren't just glasses.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:57.880
They were also restraints!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.710
If she didn't draw comics!

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.440
If she didn't draw comics, Harumi—!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:33.440
What are you, Gachableep?

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.310
Comics are interesting too.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.790
It's pretty slovenly just dropping your glasses.

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:43.020
Heavy!

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:08.710
You have a cold?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.060
You should take some medicine.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:11.820
Okay.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.690
Did the medicine not work?

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.690
It won't work immediately.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:33.410
It seems like the medicine's working... I feel a little better.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:34.840
That's good.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.800
Why didn't it work sooner!?

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.410
Isn't that surprising!?

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:43.090
There's a time lag between taking the medicine and when it works.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.100
Well, it's not limited to medicine; generally, things have—

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.090
A time lag.

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:51.190
Like broadcast of anime out in the boonies,

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:54.960
or the time between pressing the button on a digital camera and when the shutter actually closes,

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:57.730
or the time between when you eat and when you feel full.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.850
That kind of normal time lag occurs,

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.370
but beyond that,

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:18.330
Current stop, Nakano, Nakano

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.080
there's <i>that</i>.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.660
Eww.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:30.060
How disgusting! Stop grinning and remembering that.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.580
What do you mean, "how disgusting"!?

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.520
What are you doing all of a sudden!?

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:55.800
Like you can just shrug it off!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.520
Hello!

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:02.380
Man, you sure look like a hardware salesman.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:03.500
Yeah, I guess.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:09.370
I couldn't think of anything else at the time,

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:12.370
but it had me on pins and needles all night!

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.640
What's up with that remembered anger!?

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.720
There are people who have a time lag to anger.

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:20.820
You were there?

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.010
Yes, always.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:25.960
Like parents who aren't concerned at all the night before,

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:28.660
but the next morning burn with rage.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.460
Sit right there!

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:31.270
We have new products!

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.060
Would you like to try one?

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.800
How about it?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.870
Would you like to try one?

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.620
When I see a dirty book or something at a friend's house,

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.400
sometimes when I get home I feel horny.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.380
Is that time lag?

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:01.640
Now that you mention it,

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:05.240
there's things that make me shiver when I remember them later.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.260
When I remember them now, I realize they were pretty dangerous.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.240
Sketching on asbestos with chalk.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.810
Eating plenty of gyoza last year.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.460
Playing with strange adults.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:18.000
You should realize that about strange adults even then.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.740
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:21.740
What?

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.800
I just remembered that time I insensitively cut in front of you, teacher!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.880
Didn't that trouble you!?

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:29.720
When?

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:30.880
Six months ago!

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:32.410
And seven months ago I—

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:33.770
It's fine!

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.780
A time-delayed apology?

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:40.590
Now that I think of it, there are things I kind of regret.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:47.390
Come on, why don't you cleanly feel sorry for them then?

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:48.650
In one ear and out the other.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:50.720
Anyway, this world—

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.440
is full of time lags!

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.440
Like the seven-year killer!

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:59.480
What's that?

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:04.920
If you get hit with this move, you don't die right there, but die seven years later!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.670
Well, I guess there was that.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.560
Teacher, that's it.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.530
What are you doing to the reader!?

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.130
It's the seven-year laugher!

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.780
It hits them right in the funny bone,

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.030
and makes them laugh seven years later!

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.700
Don't forget to laugh seven years from now.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:24.220
That's meaningless if they don't find it funny now!

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.470
Or the other way around.

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:28.980
If they wonder why they found it funny back then...

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:32.070
It's a time lag of several years before they realize it was dull!

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:36.000
Selling to nerds after that delay is the typical state of this industry!

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:38.360
Well, in the first place,

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:42.970
even the human body, between the time the eyes see something and when the brain recognizes it,

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:45.990
has a time lag. I wonder how long it is.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.990
It's a U-boat!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:52.060
Thus, even the landscape we see here is from the past!

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:55.300
Looking at you like this, even Kitsu is from the past!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.610
So the current Kitsu

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.440
may even be like this!

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.910
What a time lag!

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:06.410
The landscape I see may even be like this now!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.680
The comic you're reading now may be old,

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.750
and by now really be like this!

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:13.970
I'm in despair!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.100
This world full of time lag has left me in despair!

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:19.070
I want to be Orihime someday soon, too

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.100
It's nothing to despair about.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.620
There's reverse time lag, too, after all.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.450
When there's a baby in her before the wedding!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.220
When it's leaked on the net before it goes on sale!

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.380
Knowing what stocks will go up before it happens!

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:39.880
That's no good either!

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.600
The gag is seven years later.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.060
What a time lag!

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:54.640
Seven years from now, won't Enari be 30 years old?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.350
I'm Tanaka Yoko!

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.870
A gag came from seven years ago!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.710
Looks like someone’s getting on.

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:17.350
Kimura, are you on a journey of self-discovery too?

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:20.260
I wouldn't take that kind of illogical trip.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.900
I'm just going on vacation.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:24.290
Kaere, save me!

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:27.030
He's trying to talk to me in English!

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:28.910
Can't you speak English too?

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:35.980
I don't understand what this person is saying in English.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.490
I'm gonna sue you!

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.100
He doesn't get Kaere's English?

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.620
So she's displayed her mastery of English.

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:48.480
There are plenty of people who, though they seem fluent in English practice,

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:52.200
display their true mastery of the language when they travel overseas.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.300
Especially English teachers.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:58.920
Well, I'm sure Kaere is a girl from somewhere other than the Anglosphere.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:07.110
This isn't the bus you take to display yourself.

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:10.340
Try Tokyo Station, Yaesu South terminal 1.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:10.840
What!

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.540
I only ride that in August!

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:20.050
Teacher, let's play a game!

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.020
The Yamanote Line game!

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.990
You're showing your sorrowful normalness.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.210
Far and wide, now and then! Red things!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:29.890
Red.

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:32.460
Anything red is fine, okay?

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.600
You were there?

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.680
Okay, I'll start.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:38.800
Tomato.

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:41.120
Bloodsplatter.

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:43.280
Sunset.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:45.590
Flesh.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.090
Red fox.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.310
Baby.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:55.370
The Red Baron shows newborn babies.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.870
In a red room behind a red door.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.720
Kitsu, you're showing the darkness of your heart!

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:04.920
Showing yourself isn't necessarily bad.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:08.460
It can be a brave coming out!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.570
All right, everyone, let's let it all out!

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.570
When did it get this full?

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.670
Who has something to share?

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:19.720
Me!

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:25.950
Up until now, I've really been a no-good, negative person who finds no meaning in life!

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.080
What do you have to share?

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:29.220
Me!

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:33.170
I put myself on a pedestal, and looked for faults in others!

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:36.240
I was horrible, no-good, worthless human trash!

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:40.670
Just because I got a bit part in an anime, I thought I was popular!

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:42.840
I was mistaken, I'm really just a creepy bald perv!

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:46.130
I mistakenly thought I was cool,

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.580
but really, I'm just a guy with a ghoulish jaw!

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.210
All of us here today thought we were no-good people.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:55.320
But Positive Leader has opened our eyes!

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:00.840
By facing reality, you understand how important you are!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:05.590
We're a family. There's no need to hide our secrets.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:22.610
Find a shining path to tomorrow in the world!

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:28.940
What kind of self-improvement seminar is this!?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.260
Self-exposition has left me in despair!

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:39.620
In these circumstances, we should progress sagely, showing nothing!

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:43.760
Then, I've thought of something good.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:50.710
I've set up a body double of young master.

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:51.260
Who?

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.850
Hello, teacher.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.910
Hello.

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:57.780
No one's realizing.

00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:00.020
Of course, it's a body double.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.380
Hey, Nozomu.

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.110
You're late, Nozomu.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.650
Oh my, brother.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:06.880
Like this, Nozomu!

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:44.720
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:46.920
Matching the song, let's draw limply, okay?

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:54.870
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:54.870 --> 00:23:01.310
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:02.870
Lightning...

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:04.520
Flash!

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:06.150
Lightning...

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:07.760
Flash!

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:10.980
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:14.250
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:16.940
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.520
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:24.920
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:28.610
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:31.380
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:33.460
Bye bye!
